identifiers:
- type: doi
  value: 10.32614/CRAN.package.micronutr
abstract: Vitamin and mineral deficiencies continue to be a significant public health
  problem. This is particularly critical in developing countries where deficiencies
  to vitamin A, iron, iodine, and other micronutrients lead to adverse health consequences.
  Cross-sectional surveys are helpful in answering questions related to the magnitude
  and distribution of deficiencies of selected vitamins and minerals. This package
  provides tools for calculating and determining select vitamin and mineral deficiencies
  based on World Health Organization (WHO) guidelines found at <https://www.who.int/teams/nutrition-and-food-safety/databases/vitamin-and-mineral-nutrition-information-system>.
